+Create a file named WORKFLOW.md with the following contents: # InsuMinder — Development & Deployment Architecture
+
+## 1. System Overview
+
+InsuMinder uses a decoupled architecture separating the client-side user interface from the backend persistence layer.
+
+* **Frontend (Client):** React built with Vite.
+  * **Local:** Runs on `http://localhost:5173` via Vite Dev Server.
+  * **Production:** Deployed automatically on **Cloudflare Pages** (`https://insuminder.pages.dev`).
+* **Backend (API & Scheduler):** Node.js with Express.
+  * **Local:** Runs on `http://localhost:5000`.
+  * **Database (Local):** SQLite (`insuminder.db`) stored directly in the project directory.
+* **Agent Integration:** Aider with local LLM (`qwen2.5-coder:7b`) managing code generation, refactoring, and atomic Git commits.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Project Directory Structure
+
+```text
+InsuMinder/
+├── client/                  # Frontend React (Vite) application
+│   ├── public/              # Static public assets (icons, manifest)
+│   ├── src/
+│   │   ├── components/      # UI components (Button, LogList, AlertCard)
+│   │   ├── services/        # API client layer (fetch / axios)
+│   │   ├── App.jsx          # Main application component
+│   │   └── main.jsx         # React DOM root entry
+│   ├── index.html           # Single Page Application HTML shell
+│   ├── package.json         # Frontend dependencies and build scripts
+│   └── vite.config.js       # Vite configuration and local proxy
+├── server/                  # Backend Node.js Express server
+│   ├── src/
+│   │   ├── db.js            # SQLite database initialization and queries
+│   │   ├── routes.js        # API endpoints (/api/injections, /api/logs)
+│   │   ├── scheduler.js     # 2h & 3h notification evaluation loop
+│   │   └── index.js         # Server entry point
+│   ├── package.json         # Backend dependencies
+│   └── insuminder.db        # SQLite database file (gitignored)
+├── .gitignore               # Excludes node_modules, .env, and local db files
+├── README.md                # General project documentation
+└── WORKFLOW.md              # Architectural & operational guidelines

